Lab 11: Managing Puppet Environments
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create and configure Puppet environments in Red Hat Satellite
Manage Puppet classes and modules effectively
Assign Puppet classes to hosts through Satellite interface
Deploy configuration changes to managed hosts using Puppet
Monitor and verify Puppet configuration deployment
Troubleshoot common Puppet environment issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux system administration
Familiarity with Red Hat Satellite concepts
Knowledge of YAML syntax and configuration files
Understanding of configuration management principles
Experience with command-line interface operations
Completed previous Satellite labs or equivalent knowledge
