Task 3: Deploy Configuration Changes via Puppet Through Satellite
Subtask 3.1: Create Custom Puppet Module
SSH to the Satellite server:
ssh root@satellite.example.com
Navigate to the Puppet modules directory:
cd /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/modules
Create a custom module structure:
# Create custom motd module
mkdir -p custom_motd/{manifests,templates,files}

# Create the main manifest
cat > custom_motd/manifests/init.pp << 'EOF'
class custom_motd {
  file { '/etc/motd':
    ensure  => file,
    content => template('custom_motd/motd.erb'),
    owner   => 'root',
    group   => 'root',
    mode    => '0644',
  }
}
EOF
Create the template file:
cat > custom_motd/templates/motd.erb << 'EOF'
=====================================
Welcome to <%= @fqdn %>
=====================================
Environment: <%= @environment %>
Managed by: Red Hat Satellite
Last Puppet Run: <%= @timestamp %>
=====================================
Unauthorized access is prohibited
=====================================
EOF
Subtask 3.2: Import New Module to Satellite
Return to Satellite web interface
Navigate to Configure → Classes
Click Import from [puppet-server]
Select production environment
Find and import the custom_motd class
Configure any necessary parameters
Subtask 3.3: Assign Custom Module to Hosts
Navigate to Hosts → All Hosts
Select client1.example.com
Edit the host and add custom_motd to Puppet classes
Save the configuration
Subtask 3.4: Trigger Puppet Run
From Satellite interface, select the host
Click Run Puppet button to trigger immediate deployment
Alternatively, use command line on the client:
# SSH to client1
ssh root@client1.example.com

# Run Puppet agent manually
puppet agent -t

# Verify the configuration was applied
cat /etc/motd
Subtask 3.5: Monitor Deployment Status
In Satellite, navigate to Monitor → Reports
View the latest Puppet run reports
Check for any errors or warnings:
# On Satellite server, check Puppet logs
tail -f /var/log/foreman/production.log

# Check Puppet server logs
tail -f /var/log/puppetlabs/puppetserver/puppetserver.log
Verify successful deployment by checking host status
Subtask 3.6: Deploy Configuration to Multiple Environments
Copy the custom module to other environments:
# On Satellite server
cp -r /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/modules/custom_motd \
      /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/development/modules/

cp -r /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/modules/custom_motd \
      /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/staging/modules/
Import classes for each environment through Satellite interface
Test deployment in development environment first
Promote successful configurations to staging, then production
Subtask 3.7: Verify Configuration Compliance
Navigate to Monitor → Configuration Status
Review compliance reports for all managed hosts
Check for configuration drift:
# On client hosts, verify Puppet is managing resources
puppet resource service httpd
puppet resource package httpd
puppet resource file /etc/motd
Address any compliance issues found
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Puppet Classes Not Importing
Symptoms: Classes don't appear in import list

Solution:

# Check Puppet server status
systemctl status puppetserver

# Verify module syntax
puppet parser validate /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/production/modules/*/manifests/*.pp

# Check Puppet server logs
journalctl -u puppetserver -f
Issue 2: Configuration Not Applying
Symptoms: Puppet runs complete but changes not applied

Solution:

# Run Puppet in debug mode
puppet agent -t --debug

# Check for certificate issues
puppet cert list --all

# Verify host can communicate with Puppet server
telnet satellite.example.com 8140
Issue 3: Environment Conflicts
Symptoms: Wrong environment configurations applied

Solution:

# Check host environment assignment
puppet config print environment

# Verify environment exists on server
ls -la /etc/puppetlabs/code/environments/

# Update host environment in Satellite interface
Verification Steps
Verify Environment Creation:
# Check environments exist
curl -k -u admin:password https://satellite.example.com/api/environments
Verify Class Assignment:
# Check host classes
puppet config print classes
Verify Configuration Deployment:
# Check last Puppet run
puppet agent --configprint lastrunfile
cat $(puppet agent --configprint lastrunfile)
